uired","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (town ~7,900 ft, Snowmass base ~8,104 ft, Highland Bowl 12,392 ft - AMS real, hike adds exertion; acclimatize, hydrate, descend if worsening); AVALANCHE backcountry/Highland-Bowl edges/snowcat terrain - CAIC ''Aspen'' zone daily bulletin (by ~4:30 PM), beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes; tree-wells; cold + intense UV; CO-82 Independence Pass CLOSED in winter (access down-valley CO-82); Traction/Chain Law - check CDOT cotrip.org"},"timing":{"peak":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' Week (ultra-luxury peaks) + X Games week (late Jan); powder heart Jan-Mar","shoulder":"early season (late Nov-mid Dec), Jan midweek outside X Games, April spring skiing","green":"May-Jun + Oct-Nov lull; summer festival season is its own high","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Little Nell/ultra-villas 6-12 mo; X Games 4-8 mo; regular winter 3-6 mo; spring 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"spring skiing; summer Aspen Music Festival + Food & Wine Classic + Maroon Bells hiking","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, Presidents'' Week, X Games (23-25 Jan 2026); summer Food & Wine (19-21 Jun 2026), Aspen Music Festival (1 Jul-23 Aug 2026) - verify","campaign_start":"FIRE spring early-bird (Mar-Jun) Ikon on-sale + ultra pre-book (6-12 mo peak); fire again Sep-Nov; summer festivals from Feb-Mar"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski four mountains on one pass","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"Aspen advance ticket (dynamic); package far better value","timing":"ski late Nov-Apr","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Aspen Mountain, Aspen Highlands, Buttermilk and Snowmass, all on a single Aspen Skiing Company lift ticket / Ikon Pass — officially 5,700+ acres combined","si":"ski","blurb":"Aspen Mountain, Aspen Highlands, Buttermilk and Snowmass, all on a single Aspen Skiing Company lift ticket / Ikon Pass — officially 5,700+ acres combined","when":"ski late Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC/ski-op 10-15% (embedded-capable)"},{"name":"The Snowmass 4,406 ft vertical"