  ('big-sky-montana', '12A', 'Big Sky', 'United States', 'One of America''s biggest mountains', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","romance","adventure","family","culinary","wellness","entertainment"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Big Sky = Boyne Resorts / Ikon; Lone Peak summit 11,166 ft, base ~7,400-7,500 ft, VERTICAL 4,350 ft; 5,850 acres, 320 trails, 40 lifts (2 gondolas + tram); combines former Moonlight Basin + Spanish Peaks (both acquired 2013) as one resort","The NEW Lone Peak Tram is operational (replaced the 1995 15-passenger tram; replacement announced 2022); all lift tickets include unlimited daily tram access - DO NOT publish old 15-person specs (new capacity/opening date unverified)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: ''Biggest Skiing in America'' (~5,850 ac) is CONTESTED - Park City (~6,700 ac) is the largest lift-served; Boyne calls Big Sky ''second-largest''. Quote acreage, not the superlative. No per-resort skier count published","Terrain ~21% beginner base up to 11% expert + 8% extreme off Lone Peak; ~400 in snow (resort figure; OnTheSnow lists 265 - flag); no night skiing; acreage-per-skier among the most generous in US skiing (uncrowded)","BZN (Bozeman Yellowstone Intl, Montana''s busiest) ~45 mi / ~1 hr N via US-191 Gallatin Canyon; ~midway to West Yellowstone (~45 mi) - a two-season Yellowstone-gateway basecamp","Luxury base: Montage Big Sky (100 rooms, ski access, golf; opening yr verify) + historic Lone Mountain Ranch (all-inclusive guest ranch, 25 cabins, 80+ km Nordic) + Summit Hotel; One&Only Moonlight Basin REPORTED but UNCONFIRMED (verify)","Strong dining scene: Everett''s 8800 (fine dining at 8,800 ft), Peaks Chophouse, M by the Alinea Group (culinary residency), Umbrella Bar (360 glass), Vista Hall food hall","NO on-site cat/heli (lift-served incl tram; backcountry via third-party guides; Nordic at Lone Mountain Ranch); NO natural hot springs at resort (Norris ~1.5-2 hr day-trip); Big Sky PBR bull-riding week in July; Ikon/lift prices dynamic"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Big Sky Medical Center (Bozeman Health) in Big Sky - 24/7 ER (operator/level/address blocked - verify); larger facilities in Bozeman (~1 hr)","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~7,400-7,500 ft, Lone Peak 11,166 ft GENUINELY HIGH; tram tops 11,000 - hydrate, ease alcohol, descend if AMS worsens); AVALANCHE backcountry - Gallatin National Forest Avalanche Center (GNFAC, mtavalanche.com), Southern Madison / Gallatin zone - VERIFY exact zone (page 403); beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes; STEEP/EXTREME Lone Peak couloirs + no-fall zones off the tram (respect closures); US-191 Gallatin Canyon winter driving + WILDLIFE on road; tree-wells; cold + intense UV"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK, Presidents'' Week, Jan-Feb powder) + big summer peak (July: Yellowstone + Big Sky PBR week)","shoulder":"early Dec (pre-holiday) + April spring skiing","green":"late spring (May) + fall (Oct-Nov) between the winter + Yellowstone seasons","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Montage/Lone Mountain Ranch 3-6 mo (holidays longer); July Yellowstone/PBR far ahead; luxury earliest","off_season_specials":"April spring skiing; whole summer Yellowstone season + PBR; midweek value; Lone Mountain Ranch Nordic","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'', spring break; summer Big Sky PBR (July 16-18, 2026 - verify) + Yellowstone traffic","campaign_start":"FIRE spring early-bird (Apr-Jun) Ikon renewals + summer-Yellowstone/PBR pre-book; fire winter again Sep-Nov"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski one of the biggest mountains in America","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"window dynamic; package best value","timing":"ski Nov-Apr","draw_rank":1,"hook":"5,850 acres of largely uncrowded terrain across